Subject: Cantor Field Attention Fault Assurance P0 Exploded Specification

@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-18_field_attention_fault_assurance\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [base] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Field_Attention_Delineation_Latch_P0.sop

& [Delineation] separates report validity from evidentiary assurance
  + validity means the retained report satisfies one closed replay contract
  + assurance names which facts that replay actually reconstructs
  + neither status establishes correspondence with unretained external state

& [SevenFoldExplosion] closes the distinction
  + [identity] every verification result carries one finite assurance class
  + [relationship] assurance is derived from terminal class and retained failed-exchange position
  + [condition] a fault is response-backed only when the failing response recomputes the exact fault text
  + [transformation] existing reports remain byte-identical while verifier output gains an explicit classification
  + [process] validate identity field events exchanges lineage terminal then emit assurance
  + [evidence] deterministic fixture stored provider response-backed fault and structural-only fault remain distinct
  + [boundary] structural-only faults preserve declarations without claiming their external cause was replayed

& [Falsification] is concrete
  + removing the failed response from a canonical runtime fault changes assurance to structural-only
  + changing a retained failed response or its fault text rejects rather than downgrades
  + completed rejected and control reports cannot claim deterministic or fault assurance
  + fixture reports cannot claim provider evidence
